+# Cache Eviction Policy
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use LRU (Least Recently Used) as the cache eviction policy, with a cache time-to-live (TTL) of 300 seconds. The choice favors simple recency-based eviction, which is predictable for workloads with temporal locality and needs less bookkeeping than frequency tracking.
